<!-- Guiding Pillars for AI Data Foundation -->
<section class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 space-y-16">
  <div>
    <div class="kube-home-section-heading mb-8">
      <div>
        <span class="kube-kicker">Core Principles</span>
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 [data-theme=dark]:text-white mt-1">
          What We Stand For
        </h2>
      </div>
      <p class="text-slate-500 max-w-md">
        Five guiding principles directing every tutorial, benchmark evaluation, and catalog entry published by the foundation.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
      <div class="kube-learning-card">
        <span class="kube-learning-step">Pillar 01 · Interoperability</span>
        <h3>Open Protocols & Tooling</h3>
        <p>
          We champion standards like the Model Context Protocol (MCP) and open-source frameworks to ensure AI systems remain modular, interoperable, and free from proprietary vendor lock-in.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="kube-learning-card">
        <span class="kube-learning-step">Pillar 02 · Transparency</span>
        <h3>Reproducible Benchmarks</h3>
        <p>
          Evaluation matters. We provide transparent scoring, hardware VRAM requirements, and quantization benchmarks so engineers make data-driven decisions when deploying models.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="kube-learning-card">
        <span class="kube-learning-step">Pillar 03 · Practice</span>
        <h3>Hands-on, Self-Paced Labs</h3>
        <p>
          Real understanding comes from building. Our labs walk through concrete implementations: setting up local vector stores, chaining LLM agents, and measuring data quality.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="kube-learning-card">
        <span class="kube-learning-step">Pillar 04 · Security</span>
        <h3>AI Safety & Data Protection</h3>
        <p>
          Security is foundational. We prioritize prompt injection defense, model watermarking, automated red-teaming, data provenance, and regulatory compliance in every tool, lab, and benchmark we publish.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="kube-learning-card">
        <span class="kube-learning-step">Pillar 05 · Open Core</span>
        <h3>Community & Open Governance</h3>
        <p>
          All foundation assets, markdown documentation, tool directories, and static files are released under the Apache 2.0 license and managed openly on GitHub.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="kube-contribute p-8 sm:p-12 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white [data-theme=dark]:border-slate-800 [data-theme=dark]:bg-slate-900 flex flex-col md:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-8">
    <div class="space-y-2 max-w-2xl">
      <span class="kube-kicker">Architecture & Foundation</span>
      <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 [data-theme=dark]:text-white">
        Open Engineering & High-Performance Architecture
      </h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 [data-theme=dark]:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        This platform is engineered using Elixir and the Phoenix framework for blazingly fast response times, high reliability, and reproducible open intelligence. Every lab, benchmark dataset, tool catalogue, article, and open-source asset is curated for the global AI community.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/tools" class="kube-button text-sm">
        Browse Tools →
      </a>
      <a href="/labs" class="kube-button kube-button-outline text-sm">
        Browse Labs →
      </a>
      <a href="/security" class="kube-button kube-button-outline text-sm">
        Security Hub →
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>